WEBVTT

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:54.000
Good evening. Thank you all for being with us today. My name is

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:59.000
Kat. My pronouns are she and her. And we're so happy that you've

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:04.000
chosen to be with us, whether this is your first time here or

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.000
your first time in a long time. We're so happy that you're here.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:14.000
Our kids ministry is hosting a fall fest for families to have

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:19.000
fun and connect on Friday, October 17th. If you have kids

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:24.000
through the sixth grade, please save the date for this fun night

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:30.000
at the Runford home here in Sachse. There will be game snacks

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:37.000
as well as pumpkin carving contest or pumpkin painting for the

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:42.000
littles. Scan the QR code to RSVP. We'd love to have you. The

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.000
sixth anniversary of the table is coming up in November, and to

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:54.000
do that, we are doing an annual chili cook off after service on

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.000
November 2nd. If you would like to show off your favorite chili

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:04.000
recipe, you can scan the QR code and sign up. And our next service

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:09.000
day for five Lowe's food pantry will be Saturday, December 6th

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:16.000
at 915 a.m. to 12. If you would like information and volunteer to

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:22.000
work in the five Lowe's food pantry, please scan the QR code and

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:28.000
sign up. We'd appreciate that. These candles are a sign of the

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.000
presence of Christ among us, fully divine but fully human. Now I

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:43.000
will call you into worship. We're going to exit the kingdom of

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:52.000
noise, hurry and productivity, and now we enter into the kingdom of

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:00.000
silence, stillness and grace. Now we enter sacred space, a space for

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:06.000
prayer, worship, and adoration, a space to encounter Christ,

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:16.000
revelation of God, heartbeat of creation. Allow the unforced

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:24.000
rhythms of grace to find you, to mend your heart. May we all come

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:30.000
home. Thank you, Kat. I see a couple of faces that I don't recognize,

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:38.000
so just real quickly I wanted to introduce ourselves. I'm Mindy. This

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:43.000
is my twin sister Maggie, in case you feel like you're seeing double.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:48.000
And this is Gary. And we're here not to, you know, put on a

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:53.000
performance for you, but hoping that we can help create a space all

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:58.000
around us that we believe kind of anchor us in to who God is and the

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:03.000
love that he has for us. So if you guys want to stand with us and

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:08.000
worship, if you're able, or you can sit back and take it in, whatever

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:13.000
you're comfortable with, we just want you to know that you're welcome in

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:18.000
this space, and we just encourage you to utilize it however you need to

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:23.000
for the love that God has for us and who loves us.

